    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d12">

                <pb facs="0054" n="26" xml:id="pg26"/>

                <head>12. Telegram From the Embassy in Iran to the Department of State<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d12-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Tehran</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1964-04-06T16:15:00+03:30">April 6, 1964, 4:15 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <p>882. Ayatollah Khomeini, at first imprisoned and later under house detention in
                    connection 1963 Moharam riots and widely regarded as leading contender for
                    position of Shia paramount leader, was released April 5 and returned to
                    religious center of Qom. Press giving minimum play. [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >less than 1 line of source text not declassified</hi>] reports (1) millahs
                    flocking to Qom from all over Iran to “kiss hands“, and (2) one tank battalion
                    concentrated Qom outskirts as precautionary measure. No info whether Khomeini
                    reached agreement with govt regarding any restriction on his future activities.
                    Embassy [<hi rendition="#italic">less than 1 line of source text not
                        declassified</hi>] contacts with good connections in religious community
                    view release as victory for Khomeini but also as wise policy decision by regime
                    in preparation for Moharam, period of deep mourning starting May 13.</p>
                <p>Request Baghdad and Karachi report any clerical reaction Khomeini’s release.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold"> Holmes </hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d12-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d12-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, POL 23–9 IRAN. Confidential. Repeated
                    to Baghdad and Karachi.</p>
            </note>
